Edit, debug and manage code with a lightweight editor and huge extension library

Visual Studio Code is Microsoft's code editor. It combines a fast, lightweight editor with features usually found in full IDEs, such as code completion, debugging and built-in Git, and grows through a large marketplace of extensions for almost any language or workflow. This is an unofficial AppImage that repacks Microsoft's own Linux release, rebuilt automatically when a new stable version comes out.

- IntelliSense code completion and navigation for many languages
- Built-in debugger with breakpoints, call stacks and an interactive console
- Git integration for staging, committing, diffs and branches
- Integrated terminal inside the editor window
- Thousands of extensions for languages, themes, linters and tools
- AI chat and coding assistance with GitHub Copilot
